# Source and docs: normalise to LF in the repository.
* text=auto

# Generated artefacts are compared byte-for-byte against a fresh `generate`
# and against a committed model cache, so git must never rewrite their line
# endings on checkout. Marking them binary keeps the bytes in the repo exactly
# equal to the bytes the generator produces, on every platform.
#
# Without this, `* text=auto` stored the CSVs as LF while csv.writer emitted
# CRLF, so "byte-identical" was true on Windows and false on Linux -- which is
# how CI caught it. See F15 in DECISIONS.md.
data/raw/*.csv       -text
data/truth/*.csv     -text
data/truth/*.json    -text
data/llm_cache/*.json -text
